nDecisions.text:
REVISED · S2, S3, P2. Problems: 'the scheduler waits on each one' was too broad; plans were partial; purchases were missing; declining had no visible consequence.
Now:
- every card shows what it blocks, what continues and what it enables, and is marked required or optional;
- it is the same decision object as the journey's checkpoint;
- retry and route previews refresh from the server when the selection changes;
- a verified purchase offer keeps approval, external payment, copy provided and copy verified apart;
- a history lists declined, deferred and obsolete decisions with their consequence.
NEEDS BACKEND: every action (decision, offer and campaign records; writer lock; authentication).

nDesk.text:
REVISED · R2, R7. Problems: an overstated interpretation sat among usable results; signing eligibility was incomplete; the signer lacked context.
Now:
- only results whose interpretation check passed are 'usable' (evidence.USABLE_REVIEW). Overstated and not-applicable annotations sit in 'Not used in this profile', with the reviewer's reasons;
- each card labels two dimensions: relation to the question, and the interpretation check;
- context fields per kind (method: support type) plus class, linked versions and limitations;
- results, annotations and distinct sources are counted per class;
- the initial state has no verdict selected; the eligibility list covers verdict, rationale ≥120 trimmed characters, identity and server checks; 'opened' is navigation and is kept apart from the reading attestation.
AVAILABLE NOW: profile, results, review labels and adjudication card (read).
NEEDS BACKEND: web signing (authentication, signer field, write path).
